<title>UK: Biocompatibles gets FDA go-ahead for lens.</title>
<headline>Biocompatibles gets FDA go-ahead for lens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British medical products group Biocompatibles International Plc said on Thursday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration had granted permission to market its new Proclear Compatibles monthly replacement contact lens in the U.S..</p>
<p>The lens will be marketed by Biocompatibles Eyecare Inc. and the permission is effective immediately. Biocompatibles said the lens, already launched in Britain and northern Europe, would be introduced in the U.S. this month.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
